WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.150
Seven numbers, sorted but rotated, and you need the smallest.

00:09.150 --> 00:14.700
Scanning all seven works, but slowly.

00:15.000 --> 00:23.092
Instead, compare the middle with the right end.

00:23.092 --> 00:31.700
That single check names the half holding the drop.

00:32.000 --> 00:39.233
7 beats 2, so the drop sits right of mid.

00:39.233 --> 00:47.700
The left half goes, and the search space halves.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.064
Halve again and again: O(log n).

00:55.064 --> 00:59.700
That’s binary search.

